# scripts/release.sh is FROZEN — do not touch

`scripts/release.sh` must remain byte-for-byte identical to its 2026.8.5.5
state, forever. Do NOT:

- edit its contents (not even comments or whitespace)
- rename, move, or delete it
- change its file mode (no chmod), ownership, or line endings
- add it to any chmod/format/lint sweep, refactor, or codemod

## Why

Fleet devices running pre-2026.8.7 builds have this exact path mode-dirty
(an old `fix_repo_permissions` chmod bug) and have no blocker-clearing code.
Any upstream change to this path makes their `git pull --ff-only` OTA abort,
stranding them on old versions permanently.

## What to do instead

- Release tooling lives in `scripts/dev-release.sh` — make changes there.
- If a task seems to require changing `scripts/release.sh`, stop and ask the
  user; do not proceed on your own.
